      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it's contested, but even if you call it \"controversial,\" can it really be considered \"legitimate legal theory\" if it relies on finding rights that have zero basis in the actual text of the Constitution? like, if a theory requires judges to essentially \"discover\" rights that aren't there to protect against \"tyranny,\" doesn't that move it out of the realm of law and into the realm of pure policy-making?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
